  "knowledgePattern": "Track a sideways parabola through ordered reflection and non-origin rotation",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Track the vertex through the first two moves",
      "body": "<p>Read the vertex of the sideways parabola. Move it upwards as stated, then reflect it in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. Track which way the parabola opens as well.</p>",
      "recap": "A reflection places a point the same distance on the other side of its mirror line.",
      "pitfall": "A vertical mirror line changes the horizontal coordinate, not the height.",
      "pause": "Sketch the vertex and opening direction after the reflection.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l12",
          "reminder": "A reflection places a point the same distance on the other side of its mirror line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rotate around the given point",
      "body": "<p>Measure from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> to the vertex you now have. For a clockwise quarter-turn, right becomes down and up becomes right.</p>",
      "recap": "Rotate distances measured from the stated centre, not from the origin.",
      "pitfall": "Add the centre coordinates back after turning those distances.",
      "pause": "Find the final vertex and opening direction, then write and expand the new parabola equation.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b4-l05",
          "reminder": "Rotate distances measured from the stated centre, not from the origin."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The original vertex is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and the parabola opens right. Translating upwards gives vertex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Reflecting in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> maps its horizontal coordinate to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>, so the vertex becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and the parabola opens left.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> Relative to the rotation centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, the vertex displacement is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. A clockwise quarter-turn maps <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, so this becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and the new vertex is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. The left-opening direction becomes upward-opening.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> The unit coefficient is unchanged by these rigid motions. The equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></math>. Answer A.</p><p><strong>4.</strong> Coordinate check: an original point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> finishes at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> into the original equation gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p>"
}
